  "modified": "2026-09-09T10:58:16Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: Unbounded memory retention in the DTLS record layer.\n     dtls1_buffer_record() adopted the entire live read buffer for every queued\n     record and allocated a fresh one, so a peer could pin roughly 17.7 KB of\n     heap per queued record regardless of how small the record actually was,\n     up to the 100-entry queue limit, exhausting memory on the endpoint.\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-54874.patch: copy only the received record into\n       a right-sized allocation and restore it on retrieval, leaving the live\n       read buffer in place, in ssl/d1_pkt.c, ssl/d1_lib.c and ssl/dtls1.h.\n     - CVE-2026-54874",
